@{ ViewBag.Title="How HGRAS works"; }
<main><section class="pgh-page-banner"><div class="pgh-wrap"><p class="pgh-eyebrow">A clearer way to share</p><h1>From hospital need<br />to confirmed handover.</h1><p>Every resource movement has a responsible team and a recorded history.</p></div></section><div class="pgh-wrap pgh-page-grid"><section class="pgh-content"><div class="help-step"><span>01</span><div><h2>Join your hospital group</h2><p>Your group administrator assigns your registered account a hospital and network role. Group administrators add facilities, departments and responsible officers.</p></div></div><div class="help-step"><span>02</span><div><h2>Record verified inventory</h2><p>Stores officers record stock by hospital and lot, with units, expiry, handling instructions, minimum reserves and reorder levels. Check each record's timestamp before relying on its count.</p></div></div><div class="help-step"><span>03</span><div><h2>Find a safe allocation</h2><p>Search the inventory for what your hospital needs. Submit a transfer request against eligible stock, choosing the receiving hospital, quantity, urgency and suitability requirements.</p></div></div><div class="help-step"><span>04</span><div><h2>Approve and dispatch</h2><p>The supplying hospital checks suitability and delivery feasibility. Approval reserves stock atomically; dispatch records transport and subtracts it from the supplying inventory.</p></div></div><div class="help-step"><span>05</span><div><h2>Receive and reconcile</h2><p>The receiving hospital inspects the delivery and records the usable quantity received. Missing or unusable units belong in the receipt note. Only accepted units enter destination stock. Both hospitals receive in-app updates and an audit history.</p></div></div><a class="pgh-button" href="@Url.Action("Index","Network")">Open hospital network →</a></section><aside class="pgh-info-card"><img class="pgh-info-image" src="@Url.Content("~/Content/img/hgras/clinical-team.jpg")" alt="Clinical team coordinating care"/><h2>People make the final decision.</h2><p>Availability suggestions do not replace clinical judgement, credential checks or approved handling procedures.</p><p>Equipment, staff, capacity and procurement modules are recorded coordination registers. Refresh the workspace to retrieve the latest saved information.</p><a class="pgh-text-link" href="@Url.Action("Contact")">Find your responsible officer →</a></aside></div></main>
